  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening regional architecture</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia is supporting ASEAN to respond to regional challenges including through capacity building activities between the ASEAN Secretariat and the Australian Public Service Commission (APSC). In December 2023, the APSC hosted 12 officials from the ASEAN Secretariat and ASEAN Member States in Canberra for a study visit focused on &#x2018;positioning the workforce for the future&#x2019;. Over four days, participants learned from technical APSC experts on core workforce functions including employee retention, workforce research, workforce planning, inclusion strategies, the use of artificial intelligence, future skills and capabilities, and performance management. The visit enhanced the policy skills of participants through sharing Australia&#x2019;s experience and promoting good governance principles. By supporting the ASEAN Secretariat to build the capabilities and establish the systems to enable a high-performing workforce, the visit enhanced the ASEAN Secretariat&#x2019;s capacity to respond to regional challenges.</narrative>
    </description>
